1
00:00:03,794 --> 00:00:05,505
"There we go.
What a good baby."

2
00:00:05,713 --> 00:00:07,006
"What a good baby boy."

3
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:09,217
"What a good baby boy."

4
00:00:10,009 --> 00:00:14,931
"Yes. Yes, I know.
You like that butterfly? Huh?"

5
00:00:18,559 --> 00:00:19,602
I could be late again.

6
00:00:20,394 --> 00:00:22,230
I'm gonna leave a check
for this week in the kitchen, okay?

7
00:00:22,355 --> 00:00:23,397
Okay.

8
00:00:23,606 --> 00:00:24,649
Hey.

9
00:00:25,733 --> 00:00:26,776
Hey.

10
00:00:27,276 --> 00:00:29,070
Now you repeat after me,
little man--

11
00:00:29,403 --> 00:00:32,615
I will not throw food
at Tina again.

12
00:00:33,241 --> 00:00:34,742
Well, I tried.

13
00:00:35,826 --> 00:00:37,245
Oh, don't worry.
He's a good boy.

14
00:00:37,703 --> 00:00:40,748
Like his father. Here we go.
Want a piece of cracker?

15
00:00:41,249 --> 00:00:42,291
Yes.

16
00:00:56,514 --> 00:00:58,099
I'm Agent Jurmain.
This is Agent Weber.

17
00:00:58,349 --> 00:00:59,392
We're gonna be your ride today.

18
00:01:04,564 --> 00:01:06,691
- Come on.
- Hey, rules are rules.

19
00:01:07,692 --> 00:01:09,777
He's a cop.
Not in front of his kid.

20
00:01:14,782 --> 00:01:16,325
All right. Let's go.

21
00:01:43,728 --> 00:01:45,187
- Agent LaRoche.
- Lisbon.

22
00:01:46,522 --> 00:01:47,565
Jane.

23
00:01:47,982 --> 00:01:50,776
Hmm, yes. The man
that watches the watchmen.

24
00:01:51,485 --> 00:01:52,528
How's tricks?

25
00:01:52,737 --> 00:01:53,779
You tell me.

26
00:01:54,071 --> 00:01:56,657
Oh, you'll get nothing from me, copper.
I'm no rat.

27
00:01:56,949 --> 00:01:59,368
My team and I will cooperate
in any way we can.

28
00:01:59,702 --> 00:02:00,745
We've got nothing to hide.

29
00:02:00,953 --> 00:02:02,538
Just better things
to do with our day.

30
00:02:07,251 --> 00:02:08,836
Ah. The man of the hour.

31
00:02:09,211 --> 00:02:10,755
Excuse me.

32
00:02:11,756 --> 00:02:12,798
You're excused.

33
00:02:20,473 --> 00:02:22,308
If I don't like
what you have to say

34
00:02:22,516 --> 00:02:26,062
you could walk out of this room
charged with murder.

35
00:02:26,771 --> 00:02:28,189
Do you understand that?

36
00:02:28,856 --> 00:02:29,899
Yes.

37
00:02:31,067 --> 00:02:32,109
Very well.

38
00:02:33,736 --> 00:02:38,449
Let's begin with your arrival
in Carson Springs a week ago.

39
00:02:39,075 --> 00:02:40,785
I got the call
around 3:00 in the morning.

40
00:02:41,369 --> 00:02:43,079
It was a shooting death
on the edge of town.

41
00:02:43,913 --> 00:02:45,623
"I arrived about 5:00 a.m."

42
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:48,334
"Jane and Lisbon were
around 20 minutes behind."

43
00:03:01,514 --> 00:03:02,556
What have we got?

44
00:03:02,723 --> 00:03:04,225
Victim's name is Andy Huff.

45
00:03:04,433 --> 00:03:06,143
Found three shotgun shells
over there.

46
00:03:08,270 --> 00:03:09,313
Nice ride.

47
00:03:09,438 --> 00:03:11,315
It's perfectly restored
except for the pellet holes.

48
00:03:11,982 --> 00:03:13,734
- Does he live nearby?
- He lives downtown.

49
00:03:14,026 --> 00:03:15,861
He's a barber.
Owns his own shop.

50
00:03:16,570 --> 00:03:17,947
It's a strange place to stop.

51
00:03:18,072 --> 00:03:20,658
Yeah, the local P.D. says the city
has a pretty big drug trade.

52
00:03:20,991 --> 00:03:23,494
Couple big gangs run it.
The Overtons and the, uh...

53
00:03:23,953 --> 00:03:25,913
Low-Riders
have the town split in two.

54
00:03:26,205 --> 00:03:28,457
- Doesn't look like a gang member.
- He's got no record, either.

55
00:03:28,749 --> 00:03:30,710
Customer maybe?
Drug deal gone wrong?

56
00:03:31,460 --> 00:03:33,421
- We should ask the other guy.
- The other guy?

57
00:03:38,217 --> 00:03:39,260
What other guy?

58
00:03:40,511 --> 00:03:42,012
A towel's missing.

59
00:03:43,681 --> 00:03:45,266
Our towel thief.

60
00:03:45,599 --> 00:03:47,351
Another victim, or it's the shooter?

61
00:03:47,601 --> 00:03:48,644
Beats me.

62
00:03:53,315 --> 00:03:54,900
We've got a wounded man
who's left the scene.

63
00:03:55,151 --> 00:03:58,112
Alert the local hospitals to be
on the lookout for a gunshot victim.

64
00:04:03,993 --> 00:04:05,244
The attack was hours ago.

65
00:04:05,578 --> 00:04:07,329
Whoever it was
could be miles from here.

66
00:04:07,830 --> 00:04:09,290
Wounded people,
they don't wanna run.

67
00:04:09,457 --> 00:04:10,833
They, uh, wanna hide.

68
00:04:17,131 --> 00:04:19,467
This is the California Bureau
of Investigation!

69
00:04:19,884 --> 00:04:21,427
We know you're in there!

70
00:04:21,802 --> 00:04:22,845
"Go away!"

71
00:04:23,804 --> 00:04:25,598
"I got a gun, and I'll shoot!"

72
00:04:25,931 --> 00:04:27,266
Uh, I'm gonna be back here.

73
00:04:28,392 --> 00:04:29,435
I'm coming in!

74
00:04:29,727 --> 00:04:30,770
Rigsby!

75
00:04:43,574 --> 00:04:45,326
Throw out your weapon.
Now!

76
00:04:46,243 --> 00:04:47,703
You go straight to hell.

77
00:04:48,829 --> 00:04:49,872
Dad?

78
00:04:53,167 --> 00:04:54,585
What the hell did you do, Dad?

79
00:04:58,589 --> 00:04:59,965
Hello to you, too, son.

80
00:05:13,227 --> 00:05:15,896
"We have dealt
with your father before."

81
00:05:17,898 --> 00:05:22,194
Last time, I felt that you
weren't being honest with me.

82
00:05:23,529 --> 00:05:27,533
Your father is a criminal.
A violent felon.

83
00:05:28,283 --> 00:05:30,828
"Smuggling. Narcotics.
Manslaughter."

84
00:05:31,036 --> 00:05:33,789
- "Yes."
- "One-time Sergeant at Arms"

85
00:05:34,122 --> 00:05:37,000
- "of the Iron Gods motorcycle gang."
- "Yes."

86
00:05:37,835 --> 00:05:40,838
"Served time in Lompoc, San Quentin"

87
00:05:41,046 --> 00:05:42,256
- "Pelican Bay."
- "Yes."

88
00:05:42,881 --> 00:05:45,968
{\an8}"Did you know that he was living
in the Carson Springs area?"

89
00:05:46,510 --> 00:05:48,136
{\an8}"I heard he'd moved.
Didn't know where."

90
00:05:48,887 --> 00:05:52,182
{\an8}Had your relationship
with your father changed?

91
00:05:52,891 --> 00:05:53,934
{\an8}What relationship?

92
00:06:04,319 --> 00:06:05,863
{\an8}- How is he?
- He's stabilized.

93
00:06:06,446 --> 00:06:07,906
{\an8}We put four units
of blood in him.

94
00:06:08,031 --> 00:06:09,992
{\an8}He's got a couple dozen
shotgun pellets in him.

95
00:06:10,367 --> 00:06:11,577
{\an8}Most of them
shouldn't be a problem

96
00:06:11,785 --> 00:06:13,370
unless he walks
through a metal detector.

97
00:06:13,745 --> 00:06:15,998
{\an8}- Most of them?
- There's a pellet close to his heart

98
00:06:16,206 --> 00:06:17,624
{\an8}lodged in his pericardium.

99
00:06:18,292 --> 00:06:19,710
There's a chance it could fall out.

100
00:06:20,127 --> 00:06:23,171
{\an8}If it does, it could cause
cardiac arrest or a stroke.

101
00:06:23,380 --> 00:06:24,423
Well, can you get to it?

102
00:06:24,590 --> 00:06:26,008
Open-heart surgery
is too great a risk

103
00:06:26,133 --> 00:06:27,301
{\an8}especially in his condition.

104
00:06:27,885 --> 00:06:30,053
{\an8}Hopefully, scar tissue will cover it
and he'll be fine.

105
00:06:30,387 --> 00:06:33,098
{\an8}- Is there anything that can help?
- Quiet life, low heart rate.

106
00:06:33,932 --> 00:06:35,893
He should invest
in a good easy chair.

107
00:06:36,018 --> 00:06:39,104
{\an8}Avoid excitement.
Smoking. Drinking. Hard living.

108
00:06:39,813 --> 00:06:40,856
Great.

109
00:06:41,273 --> 00:06:43,734
{\an8}- Uh, can I ask him a few questions?
- Yeah. Both of us.

110
00:06:54,995 --> 00:06:56,038
{\an8}How do you feel?

111
00:06:58,498 --> 00:07:00,584
{\an8}Well, they got some
high-grade dope here.

112
00:07:01,084 --> 00:07:03,837
{\an8}- I'm fine as may wine.
- Good. That's great.

113
00:07:05,797 --> 00:07:07,007
{\an8}You know, you should have seen
the look on your face

114
00:07:07,132 --> 00:07:08,717
{\an8}when you found me
in that shack.

115
00:07:09,051 --> 00:07:10,761
{\an8}- Looked scared as hell.
- Yeah, well, I was.

116
00:07:11,345 --> 00:07:12,387
I am.

117
00:07:12,888 --> 00:07:13,931
You nearly died.

118
00:07:15,599 --> 00:07:17,768
{\an8}Not me.
I'm going when I say I go.

119
00:07:18,185 --> 00:07:20,020
{\an8}- What happened, Dad?
- Nothing.

120
00:07:21,396 --> 00:07:22,814
{\an8}Forget about it.
Ain't no big deal.

121
00:07:24,524 --> 00:07:25,943
So tell me. Boy or girl?

122
00:07:26,276 --> 00:07:29,071
{\an8}- How'd you know?
- Well, I ain't that far outta the loop.

123
00:07:29,446 --> 00:07:30,739
{\an8}Cousin Katie.

124
00:07:31,156 --> 00:07:32,699
She told me you were expecting.

125
00:07:32,950 --> 00:07:33,992
His name's Ben.

126
00:07:35,202 --> 00:07:37,120
{\an8}Is this little Ben's mama
over here?

127
00:07:37,454 --> 00:07:38,497
She's purty.

128
00:07:39,164 --> 00:07:41,333
No. This, uh, this is my boss.

129
00:07:42,125 --> 00:07:43,460
{\an8}I'm Agent Lisbon.

130
00:07:44,127 --> 00:07:45,712
{\an8}Why don't you tell us
what happened, Mr. Rigsby?

131
00:07:46,296 --> 00:07:47,506
{\an8}I gotta tell you

132
00:07:48,882 --> 00:07:51,468
I could not work
for a beautiful woman like you.

133
00:07:52,260 --> 00:07:53,762
{\an8}It's way too distracting.

134
00:07:54,888 --> 00:07:56,556
You dating anyone
right now, honey?

135
00:07:57,474 --> 00:08:00,352
Both you and the victim were hit
with shotgun pellets.

136
00:08:00,978 --> 00:08:03,981
Your pistol hadn't been fired
so you're not a suspect right now.

137
00:08:04,356 --> 00:08:05,399
You can tell us what happened.

138
00:08:05,899 --> 00:08:08,568
Years ago, I'd have probably
been too much for you.

139
00:08:09,069 --> 00:08:10,570
Hell, I'd have broke you.

140
00:08:11,613 --> 00:08:13,448
Now, the circumstances

141
00:08:13,573 --> 00:08:15,534
I bet we move
just about the same speed.

142
00:08:15,659 --> 00:08:17,035
Dad, this is serious.
You've been shot.

143
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:18,245
You need to understand
there's no more time for--

144
00:08:18,537 --> 00:08:20,664
You need to understand
that I don't need you

145
00:08:21,331 --> 00:08:24,126
or any other government
bitch fixing my problems for me.

146
00:08:25,335 --> 00:08:26,378
What about Andy Huff?

147
00:08:26,837 --> 00:08:27,879
He's dead.

148
00:08:28,422 --> 00:08:30,173
Well, then he doesn't need anything.

149
00:08:34,928 --> 00:08:36,847
The vic's business partner
should be at CBI by now.

150
00:08:37,097 --> 00:08:38,223
We can talk to her,
try to get some leads.

151
00:08:38,598 --> 00:08:39,641
- Rigsby.
- Yeah?

152
00:08:40,517 --> 00:08:42,227
Jane and I are gonna go
talk to the barber.

153
00:08:42,769 --> 00:08:45,230
- You're not working this case.
- Please, boss, I gotta do something.

154
00:08:45,355 --> 00:08:47,399
- You can stay here or you can go home.
- No way. I'm not staying here.

155
00:08:47,983 --> 00:08:49,317
I didn't give you a choice.

156
00:08:52,946 --> 00:08:53,989
It's okay.

157
00:08:54,990 --> 00:08:56,283
Go home. See your kid.

158
00:08:58,201 --> 00:08:59,244
Okay.

159
00:08:59,369 --> 00:09:02,497
We just wanna find whoever it is
that killed him, Ms. Stewart.

160
00:09:02,873 --> 00:09:03,915
People call me Stew.

161
00:09:04,875 --> 00:09:07,085
Like that matters right now.
Call me whatever.

162
00:09:09,254 --> 00:09:10,297
Sorry.

163
00:09:11,048 --> 00:09:12,340
This is a lot to take in.

164
00:09:13,008 --> 00:09:14,051
Where did you meet the victim?

165
00:09:15,677 --> 00:09:17,095
We grew up in Carson Springs.

166
00:09:18,180 --> 00:09:20,057
We managed to stay
outta the gangs and the drugs.

167
00:09:20,307 --> 00:09:22,768
- That put us in the minority.
- It's a rough town.

168
00:09:23,060 --> 00:09:24,227
Oh, you have no idea.

169
00:09:26,063 --> 00:09:27,481
Uh... we both went
to barber school.

170
00:09:28,148 --> 00:09:29,191
We were buddies

171
00:09:29,316 --> 00:09:32,277
so going into business together
was just a no-brainer.

172
00:09:34,821 --> 00:09:36,239
This is who Huff was with.

173
00:09:36,865 --> 00:09:38,825
He's an ex-con
with a violent record.

174
00:09:38,992 --> 00:09:40,160
Have you seen him before?

175
00:09:41,328 --> 00:09:42,370
No.

176
00:09:42,913 --> 00:09:45,373
Killer wounded him but didn't go
after him when he ran away.

177
00:09:46,249 --> 00:09:47,542
Like he wasn't the target.

178
00:09:49,628 --> 00:09:50,670
So?

179
00:09:51,671 --> 00:09:54,257
Well, we just told you
that your business partner

180
00:09:54,424 --> 00:09:56,259
was driving around
with a violent criminal

181
00:09:56,426 --> 00:09:57,469
and you didn't blink.

182
00:09:58,595 --> 00:09:59,638
Why not?

183
00:10:01,181 --> 00:10:02,766
I really don't wanna get involved.

184
00:10:03,391 --> 00:10:04,601
Just tell us what you know.

185
00:10:04,893 --> 00:10:06,895
You don't have to be
involved past that.

186
00:10:09,147 --> 00:10:10,190
Samantha.

187
00:10:14,111 --> 00:10:15,362
Please tell us what happened.

188
00:10:20,575 --> 00:10:22,536
Family troubles, I guess.

189
00:10:25,330 --> 00:10:27,833
We don't have any living relatives
on record.

190
00:10:28,959 --> 00:10:30,794
Tom Overton was his father.

191
00:10:31,586 --> 00:10:32,838
You know, the Overtons?

192
00:10:33,338 --> 00:10:35,382
Overtons run Carson Springs.

193
00:10:36,133 --> 00:10:39,344
Half of it, anyway.
And Tom Overton ran the family.

194
00:10:40,387 --> 00:10:42,472
He died a long time ago
of cancer.

195
00:10:43,265 --> 00:10:45,809
- Was Huff in the family business?
- No. No way.

196
00:10:47,644 --> 00:10:49,980
Um, his mom was just a kid
when she had him.

197
00:10:51,273 --> 00:10:54,234
And as soon as she saw
what kinda man Tom Overton was

198
00:10:54,484 --> 00:10:56,319
she wouldn't have nothing
to do with him.

199
00:10:57,279 --> 00:10:59,906
She raised him on her own
without a penny of Overton money.

200
00:11:00,407 --> 00:11:01,783
She raised him honest.

201
00:11:02,868 --> 00:11:04,077
Is she dead, as well?

202
00:11:04,494 --> 00:11:05,537
Car crash.

203
00:11:06,371 --> 00:11:08,874
None of the Overtons
even showed up at the funeral

204
00:11:09,082 --> 00:11:12,669
so... no,
he wasn't close with them.

205
00:11:13,128 --> 00:11:14,629
But he couldn't escape them, either?

206
00:11:16,131 --> 00:11:17,174
It's family.

207
00:11:18,216 --> 00:11:19,885
I mean, you know
how that is.

208
00:11:21,845 --> 00:11:23,138
D.A. sent over what they could.

209
00:11:23,346 --> 00:11:25,182
They've got a thick file
on Carson Springs.

210
00:11:25,682 --> 00:11:27,601
The Overtons have been selling
illegal substances in town

211
00:11:27,726 --> 00:11:28,768
since prohibition.

212
00:11:28,935 --> 00:11:30,896
Now they focus on illegal
prescriptions and meth.

213
00:11:31,271 --> 00:11:32,314
But they're not alone.

214
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:33,857
These days,
they own half the city.

215
00:11:34,065 --> 00:11:36,318
The east side belongs
to a gang called the Low-Riders

216
00:11:36,526 --> 00:11:37,569
that came along in the '80s.

217
00:11:37,819 --> 00:11:40,655
The river that runs through town
is the border between their turfs.

218
00:11:41,239 --> 00:11:42,282
That's very orderly.

219
00:11:43,033 --> 00:11:45,577
The D.E.A. says the two gangs
fought a war about ten years ago.

220
00:11:45,785 --> 00:11:47,120
People died. About 30.

221
00:11:47,412 --> 00:11:49,581
- 30?
- Including the Overton boss.

222
00:11:50,916 --> 00:11:52,709
Cutting the town in two was the only
way they would come to peace.

223
00:11:53,168 --> 00:11:54,669
It's been quiet for a long time.

224
00:11:54,920 --> 00:11:57,380
Huff and Steve were attacked
in Low-Rider territory.

225
00:11:57,881 --> 00:12:00,300
Maybe the Low-Riders
saw him as, uh, an Overton

226
00:12:00,467 --> 00:12:02,010
- decided to take him out.
- His partner said

227
00:12:02,219 --> 00:12:04,221
that he had nothing to do
with the family and I believe her.

228
00:12:04,638 --> 00:12:06,306
Maybe they don't care.
All's fair in war.

229
00:12:06,556 --> 00:12:09,142
What war? It's been quiet
between the two gangs lately.

230
00:12:09,392 --> 00:12:10,435
Why shoot someone now?

231
00:12:10,894 --> 00:12:13,355
- Let's go ask them.
- We don't have enough information.

232
00:12:13,813 --> 00:12:15,232
Local cops say there's a gym

233
00:12:15,398 --> 00:12:17,400
where a lot of the younger gang
members hang out.

234
00:12:17,525 --> 00:12:18,777
Maybe we can
learn something there.

235
00:12:19,027 --> 00:12:22,572
We'll give it a shot. Cho, you and Jane
go and talk to Steve Rigsby.

236
00:12:23,156 --> 00:12:24,574
He could be tied in
with one of these gangs.

237
00:12:24,741 --> 00:12:26,326
- Think he'll talk?
- No.

238
00:12:26,534 --> 00:12:27,911
But Jane might not need him to.

239
00:12:39,798 --> 00:12:40,924
So can you tell me if the feud

240
00:12:41,049 --> 00:12:43,009
between the Low-Riders
and the Overtons is heating up?

241
00:12:44,010 --> 00:12:45,845
- Anything?
- Sorry, lady.

242
00:12:46,179 --> 00:12:48,181
We're not allowed to talk
gang business in the gym.

243
00:12:48,807 --> 00:12:50,225
It's neutral ground.

244
00:12:51,101 --> 00:12:53,270
Hey, knucklehead.

245
00:12:53,937 --> 00:12:55,105
You bothering this lady?

246
00:12:55,981 --> 00:12:57,148
Can I help you?

247
00:12:57,482 --> 00:12:58,984
Grace Van Pelt, CBI.

248
00:12:59,567 --> 00:13:01,403
I'm working a case
that might have a gang angle.

249
00:13:01,611 --> 00:13:03,280
Just looking
for some more information.

250
00:13:04,072 --> 00:13:05,115
Fletcher Moss.

251
00:13:05,865 --> 00:13:07,409
- Nice to meet you.
- Hey.

252
00:13:08,827 --> 00:13:10,662
Andy Huff was murdered last night.

253
00:13:11,288 --> 00:13:13,748
It's all over town. I heard that.
That's terrible.

254
00:13:14,749 --> 00:13:16,668
- What happened?
- That's what we're looking into.

255
00:13:16,876 --> 00:13:19,004
We're told you have a pretty
good handle on the scene here.

256
00:13:19,462 --> 00:13:20,505
Any insights?

257
00:13:21,006 --> 00:13:23,300
Well, you know, I heard
that he was a nice guy

258
00:13:23,967 --> 00:13:25,510
uh, he was a civilian.

259
00:13:26,094 --> 00:13:27,470
How come this place
is neutral ground?

260
00:13:28,346 --> 00:13:30,598
Well, I started this place
about two years ago

261
00:13:30,849 --> 00:13:32,309
with one rule--no gangs.

262
00:13:33,351 --> 00:13:35,020
I was in gang life as a kid.

263
00:13:35,395 --> 00:13:36,896
I had to get shot and go to prison

264
00:13:37,063 --> 00:13:38,773
to knock some sense
into me, but, uh...

265
00:13:40,025 --> 00:13:41,693
I don't know.
I figure this is a better way.

266
00:13:42,485 --> 00:13:44,029
Were you an Overton
or a Low-Rider?

267
00:13:44,362 --> 00:13:46,865
Neither. I was a Cobra.
Ancient history.

268
00:13:47,324 --> 00:13:49,159
Andy was on Low-Rider turf
when he died.

269
00:13:49,826 --> 00:13:51,661
You think they would've shot him
just for being there?

270
00:13:53,288 --> 00:13:54,456
You know, back in the day

271
00:13:54,622 --> 00:13:56,750
when those guys were tearing
the town apart, I'd say yeah.

272
00:13:56,916 --> 00:13:58,543
But now it doesn't make
much sense.

273
00:13:58,752 --> 00:14:01,254
Unless the Low-Riders are looking
to start the war up again.

274
00:14:01,880 --> 00:14:03,506
You know, the Overtons
have better customers

275
00:14:03,673 --> 00:14:06,634
they got better turf, less trouble.

276
00:14:07,594 --> 00:14:08,720
Low-Riders may want it all.

277
00:14:12,849 --> 00:14:14,476
I hate the smell of hospitals.

278
00:14:14,601 --> 00:14:16,936
Everybody does.
Bad smells, bad memories.

279
00:14:17,062 --> 00:14:18,104
That's because the memory

280
00:14:18,229 --> 00:14:20,607
is right next to the smell box
inside your brain.

281
00:14:21,066 --> 00:14:23,318
Nothing makes you remember
like a smell.

282
00:14:27,822 --> 00:14:29,240
Maybe they're doing tests
or something.

283
00:14:30,992 --> 00:14:32,118
Yeah, I don't think so.

284
00:14:32,369 --> 00:14:34,120
Excuse me. Can I help you?

285
00:14:36,498 --> 00:14:38,416
There was a man attached
to this needle.

286
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:40,043
Have you seen him?

287
00:14:45,821 --> 00:14:47,656
How does a man
in his condition

288
00:14:47,906 --> 00:14:50,534
walk out of a hospital
without being noticed?

289
00:14:51,076 --> 00:14:52,911
He grabbed some clothes
from the man in the next room

290
00:14:53,036 --> 00:14:54,121
and he walked out the door.

291
00:14:55,289 --> 00:14:56,331
That's my dad.

292
00:14:57,624 --> 00:15:00,544
And so Lisbon invited you
back on the case?

293
00:15:00,711 --> 00:15:01,920
No, she didn't invite me.

294
00:15:02,087 --> 00:15:04,631
She was reluctant, but I insisted
and she warned me to be very careful.

295
00:15:04,756 --> 00:15:06,091
I-I want that clear.

296
00:15:07,050 --> 00:15:08,093
Go on.

297
00:15:09,052 --> 00:15:11,263
I took Cho
and we went to look for him.

298
00:15:12,180 --> 00:15:14,683
I talked to some biker buddies
and an old girlfriend.

299
00:15:15,225 --> 00:15:16,268
Ah, yes.

300
00:15:16,810 --> 00:15:19,604
That would be the woman
called...

301
00:15:20,314 --> 00:15:21,356
- "Rocket"?
- Yes.

302
00:15:21,898 --> 00:15:23,108
She had heard from him.

303
00:15:24,192 --> 00:15:25,527
Dad wanted to see her.

304
00:15:25,819 --> 00:15:27,738
He was waiting for her
in a bar in Carson Springs

305
00:15:27,946 --> 00:15:29,323
but she was scared,
so I went instead.

306
00:15:32,075 --> 00:15:33,118
You went?

307
00:15:34,494 --> 00:15:36,204
- Where was Cho?
- We--

308
00:15:37,873 --> 00:15:39,333
I thought it was more likely

309
00:15:39,458 --> 00:15:41,543
that he would come quietly
if I was alone.

310
00:15:43,295 --> 00:15:44,338
He doesn't like cops.

311
00:15:46,256 --> 00:15:47,507
Doesn't like anyone much.

312
00:15:55,223 --> 00:15:56,266
Here you go.

313
00:15:58,560 --> 00:15:59,936
Hey. Let's go.

314
00:16:00,562 --> 00:16:01,688
I'm taking you back
to the hospital.

315
00:16:02,105 --> 00:16:03,940
Damn. You can never trust
a woman.

316
00:16:04,066 --> 00:16:05,108
Let's go.

317
00:16:07,027 --> 00:16:09,529
Look, you can sit down
or you can get out

318
00:16:09,738 --> 00:16:10,781
but I'm good here.

319
00:16:10,906 --> 00:16:12,240
Listen, you need to be in a hospital.

320
00:16:12,449 --> 00:16:14,534
I don't believe I need
to be doing a damn thing.

321
00:16:14,910 --> 00:16:16,620
You have a shotgun pellet
lodged in your heart.

322
00:16:16,787 --> 00:16:17,954
It could come loose
at any time.

323
00:16:19,039 --> 00:16:21,583
You're just like your mother.
Worry, worry, worry.

324
00:16:21,792 --> 00:16:23,668
I thought you'd be out there
looking for the guy who shot you.

325
00:16:24,836 --> 00:16:27,464
I'd rather sit here and have another beer.
That's my choice.

326
00:16:28,048 --> 00:16:29,591
Now you make your choice.

327
00:16:30,008 --> 00:16:32,344
But I'm telling you I'm not leaving
here without a fight.

328
00:16:34,513 --> 00:16:36,181
Yeah, well, I ain't fighting
you anymore.

329
00:16:38,141 --> 00:16:40,143
Miss, I'll take a beer.

330
00:16:59,955 --> 00:17:00,997
Hi.

331
00:17:01,123 --> 00:17:02,874
Whatever it is, we're not buying.

332
00:17:03,708 --> 00:17:06,795
We're not selling.
I'm Agent Lisbon, CBI.

333
00:17:07,212 --> 00:17:08,588
This is Patrick Jane.

334
00:17:09,923 --> 00:17:10,966
I said we're not interested.

335
00:17:11,508 --> 00:17:13,093
Well, I'd love to hear that
from your boss.

336
00:17:13,593 --> 00:17:16,012
That is a very nice suit on you.
Very sharp.

337
00:17:20,142 --> 00:17:21,184
Whoa.

338
00:17:32,863 --> 00:17:34,990
Hello.
What's his name?

339
00:17:35,824 --> 00:17:37,742
- Brutus.
- Brutus.

340
00:17:38,618 --> 00:17:39,911
I'm Sue. Can I help you?

341
00:17:40,120 --> 00:17:41,788
We wanted to talk to you
about Andy Huff.

342
00:17:42,122 --> 00:17:43,290
And who says I'm your gal?

343
00:17:43,707 --> 00:17:45,125
Well, you're the boss,
aren't you?

344
00:17:45,917 --> 00:17:47,752
Dogs and humans
protect the Alpha.

345
00:17:49,045 --> 00:17:50,088
Don't worry, Rawson.

346
00:17:51,465 --> 00:17:52,883
It's fine. Come on.

347
00:18:03,935 --> 00:18:05,353
This is my son Kyle.

348
00:18:06,062 --> 00:18:08,356
Very nice to meet you, ma'am.
Sir.

349
00:18:08,648 --> 00:18:10,484
Hey, Kyle.
Strapping lad.

350
00:18:12,694 --> 00:18:15,280
Your brother Tom
he never claimed Huff as his son.

351
00:18:15,489 --> 00:18:17,199
- Did you have any contact with him?
- Nope.

352
00:18:17,991 --> 00:18:19,159
Did you kill him?

353
00:18:20,994 --> 00:18:22,496
Now why would I do that?

354
00:18:24,122 --> 00:18:25,290
He was my brother's...

355
00:18:27,042 --> 00:18:28,126
He was my brother's blood.

356
00:18:28,543 --> 00:18:30,420
I think the word
you're struggling not to say

357
00:18:30,587 --> 00:18:33,048
- is "bastard."
- He was my brother's bastard.

358
00:18:34,174 --> 00:18:36,593
And he never wanted anything
to do with me.

359
00:18:37,385 --> 00:18:38,428
I didn't kill him.

360
00:18:38,887 --> 00:18:39,930
And you don't care
that he's dead

361
00:18:40,055 --> 00:18:42,390
but you do care
that he was murdered.

362
00:18:43,058 --> 00:18:45,310
Appearances are a big thing
in your line of business.

363
00:18:45,435 --> 00:18:46,478
My line of business?

364
00:18:48,355 --> 00:18:50,106
We own some dry cleaners.

365
00:18:50,732 --> 00:18:52,317
No, I'm not talking about that.

366
00:18:53,777 --> 00:18:54,986
I'm talking about the drug dealing.

367
00:18:55,654 --> 00:18:57,656
Drug dealing?
I don't--drug...

368
00:18:58,698 --> 00:19:00,659
Huff was killed on Low-Rider turf.

369
00:19:01,076 --> 00:19:03,870
Now are you involved in some
sort of dispute with the Low-Riders?

370
00:19:04,496 --> 00:19:06,623
I--Low-Riders?
I'm... I...

371
00:19:06,873 --> 00:19:08,416
You remember them.
They killed your husband.

372
00:19:13,588 --> 00:19:14,714
I'm a businesswoman.

373
00:19:15,757 --> 00:19:16,925
Dry cleaning.

374
00:19:17,467 --> 00:19:19,844
I don't know who killed Huff
and I don't know why.

375
00:19:24,474 --> 00:19:26,434
Your rug to dry clean, I guess.

376
00:19:29,354 --> 00:19:33,358
All right, listen up. You're going
for a knockout every time, all right?

377
00:19:33,858 --> 00:19:36,152
But the punch that hurts
the most is the one that lands.

378
00:19:36,278 --> 00:19:37,946
You gotta hit 'em more,
not harder.

379
00:19:38,238 --> 00:19:39,364
It's called the Stockton slap.

380
00:19:40,240 --> 00:19:42,909
The detective's right.
It's called the Stockton slap.

381
00:19:43,702 --> 00:19:44,828
All right, give me some pushups.

382
00:19:45,120 --> 00:19:46,580
As many as you can do
plus 10.

383
00:19:47,872 --> 00:19:49,874
That's not bad.
You watch the fights?

384
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:52,085
I've been watching some.
I like how it gets to the point.

385
00:19:52,460 --> 00:19:55,463
Yeah, well, you know, with gloves
and a ref, it's not a real fight.

386
00:19:55,672 --> 00:19:57,757
- In a real fight...
- Yeah, I know. I've been in a real fight.

387
00:19:58,341 --> 00:19:59,593
What are you here for, detective?

388
00:20:00,093 --> 00:20:01,553
My boss is on her way
to meet the Low-Riders.

389
00:20:01,678 --> 00:20:02,721
I was hoping you could
help me out.

390
00:20:03,013 --> 00:20:04,472
They're led by a guy
named Beltran, right?

391
00:20:04,764 --> 00:20:05,807
That's a bad dude.

392
00:20:06,349 --> 00:20:09,185
Overtons, uh, ran this town
for a long time

393
00:20:09,311 --> 00:20:11,563
you know, and then little gangs
would pop up here and there

394
00:20:11,688 --> 00:20:14,399
no threat to them.
But Beltran stood up to them.

395
00:20:14,774 --> 00:20:16,359
So he killed
Sue Overton's husband?

396
00:20:16,610 --> 00:20:18,069
Well, I don't know
who pulled the trigger

397
00:20:18,486 --> 00:20:19,529
but yeah.

398
00:20:19,821 --> 00:20:21,698
And the Overtons killed
his little brother.

399
00:20:22,907 --> 00:20:24,326
That last war was brutal.

400
00:20:25,076 --> 00:20:26,119
You don't want a sequel.

401
00:20:38,131 --> 00:20:39,466
We're looking for Beltran.

402
00:20:40,175 --> 00:20:41,217
I didn't do it.

403
00:20:41,718 --> 00:20:44,638
- Do what?
- Whatever it is you think I did.

404
00:20:45,347 --> 00:20:47,599
Somebody killed
a relative of the Overtons.

405
00:20:49,225 --> 00:20:50,352
I sure didn't do that.

406
00:20:51,936 --> 00:20:53,188
He was on your turf.

407
00:20:53,730 --> 00:20:55,315
Maybe you saw Andy Huff

408
00:20:55,523 --> 00:20:57,150
you wanted to send a message
to the Overtons?

409
00:20:57,275 --> 00:20:58,318
A message?

410
00:20:58,860 --> 00:21:00,070
I don't know
what you're talking about.

411
00:21:00,278 --> 00:21:02,530
When the Overtons
beat him up

412
00:21:03,281 --> 00:21:04,324
that was a message.

413
00:21:04,866 --> 00:21:07,035
Question is, what was it saying?

414
00:21:09,245 --> 00:21:10,497
Those bruises are only
a few days old.

415
00:21:10,622 --> 00:21:11,956
Before the murder.

416
00:21:12,165 --> 00:21:14,584
- Was Huff payback for the beating?
- Let's get 'em outta here.

417
00:21:14,709 --> 00:21:15,752
Calm down, Joey.

418
00:21:17,545 --> 00:21:19,381
I made a mistake.
I trusted the Overtons.

419
00:21:19,547 --> 00:21:22,717
My guy paid for it but we didn't kill
Huff for any payback.

420
00:21:22,967 --> 00:21:24,636
- What does that mean?
- We're just talking here?

421
00:21:25,679 --> 00:21:26,721
Yeah, I think.

422
00:21:27,681 --> 00:21:29,015
Yeah, well, there's a new
park in town.

423
00:21:29,599 --> 00:21:31,601
A good place to maybe
set up a market.

424
00:21:31,851 --> 00:21:34,187
You know, maybe we had
a little disagreement about it.

425
00:21:34,688 --> 00:21:36,773
So the Overtons beat up your guy
over the new turf?

426
00:21:37,148 --> 00:21:38,191
I say what I gotta say.

427
00:21:39,442 --> 00:21:40,485
We didn't kill anybody.

428
00:21:41,361 --> 00:21:42,404
Not last night.

429
00:21:42,821 --> 00:21:44,906
You ever thought about just sitting
down with Sue Overton?

430
00:21:45,740 --> 00:21:47,909
Having a cup of tea, little chat?

431
00:21:48,493 --> 00:21:50,829
Look, in the last war
the Overtons killed my little brother.

432
00:21:51,746 --> 00:21:53,373
I heard that woman Sue
ordered the hit

433
00:21:53,540 --> 00:21:56,084
so, no, I am not interested
in sitting down with her, ever.

434
00:21:57,627 --> 00:21:59,212
I don't want anything to do
with those people.

435
00:21:59,462 --> 00:22:01,172
But if the Overtons
go to war with you

436
00:22:01,297 --> 00:22:02,799
then you're--you're ready
to jump right in there?

437
00:22:03,091 --> 00:22:04,134
Hell, man...

438
00:22:05,009 --> 00:22:06,052
can't be no punk.

439
00:22:08,096 --> 00:22:09,139
Right?

440
00:22:09,431 --> 00:22:10,473
All right.

441
00:22:10,890 --> 00:22:12,767
- I'm... down.
- He doesn't want to.

442
00:22:13,393 --> 00:22:16,229
Somebody killed Huff to start
the feud back up.

443
00:22:16,688 --> 00:22:17,731
We better do something

444
00:22:17,856 --> 00:22:20,066
or this town's gonna get
real bloody real fast.

445
00:22:20,608 --> 00:22:22,777
What do you think?
Did Beltran kill Huff

446
00:22:22,902 --> 00:22:24,779
to provoke the Overtons
or did Sue do it

447
00:22:24,904 --> 00:22:26,740
to have an excuse
to attack the Low-Riders?

448
00:22:27,031 --> 00:22:28,366
- Neither.
- What do you mean, neither?

449
00:22:28,491 --> 00:22:29,743
Well, Sue doesn't wanna fight
this war.

450
00:22:29,868 --> 00:22:31,828
Neither does Beltran,
but they both will fight it.

451
00:22:32,120 --> 00:22:34,456
- The question is, why?
- No, it's, who?

452
00:22:48,094 --> 00:22:49,137
Again?

453
00:22:50,597 --> 00:22:53,266
You don't like it, put your own damn
quarter in the machine.

454
00:22:55,602 --> 00:22:57,228
So you're not going
after the guy who shot you?

455
00:22:58,062 --> 00:22:59,439
Maybe I'm waiting for him here.

456
00:22:59,647 --> 00:23:00,982
Or maybe you don't know
who he is.

457
00:23:01,316 --> 00:23:02,358
Don't I?

458
00:23:03,485 --> 00:23:04,527
No.

459
00:23:04,736 --> 00:23:05,779
You don't.

460
00:23:06,404 --> 00:23:07,989
You'd already be out there
hunting him down.

461
00:23:08,865 --> 00:23:10,241
That's your code.

462
00:23:16,122 --> 00:23:17,165
I don't know anything.

463
00:23:19,250 --> 00:23:21,377
All I saw
were flashes in the dark.

464
00:23:21,544 --> 00:23:22,587
Why were you there?

465
00:23:24,506 --> 00:23:25,673
Eh, somebody called Huff.

466
00:23:26,466 --> 00:23:28,218
Said they were gonna burn down
his barbershop

467
00:23:28,426 --> 00:23:29,719
if he didn't come.

468
00:23:31,054 --> 00:23:34,390
Kid got scared, so I went to help him.
That's all I know.

469
00:23:36,893 --> 00:23:37,936
Thank you.

470
00:23:39,687 --> 00:23:40,772
Let's see some pictures.

471
00:23:54,577 --> 00:23:56,079
- Who's the mom?
- We're split up.

472
00:23:56,913 --> 00:23:58,873
Team was working a case.
I faked my own death.

473
00:23:58,998 --> 00:24:01,793
She got mad.
It's... it's complicated.

474
00:24:01,918 --> 00:24:03,419
There's more pictures
if you wanna just...

475
00:24:03,628 --> 00:24:05,004
I know how to use it.

476
00:24:07,090 --> 00:24:08,967
- It's a hell of a thing.
- Yeah, it is.

477
00:24:10,176 --> 00:24:11,344
I look at him and I feel like--

478
00:24:14,639 --> 00:24:16,099
Don't go too easy on him.

479
00:24:16,933 --> 00:24:18,518
No parenting advice.
Thanks.

480
00:24:18,768 --> 00:24:20,395
What do you got
to complain about?

481
00:24:20,812 --> 00:24:21,855
I did my job.

482
00:24:22,981 --> 00:24:24,232
You did your job?

483
00:24:24,858 --> 00:24:25,900
That's right.

484
00:24:26,693 --> 00:24:27,735
You're still here.

485
00:24:28,778 --> 00:24:30,196
You're a man of respect.

486
00:24:32,073 --> 00:24:34,450
You walk around all over the place
with a legit weapon.

487
00:24:34,576 --> 00:24:36,035
You got a handsome son.

488
00:24:37,036 --> 00:24:38,329
I did a good job.

489
00:24:39,455 --> 00:24:40,498
Yeah.

490
00:24:41,332 --> 00:24:42,876
I suppose when you look
at it like that.

491
00:24:44,502 --> 00:24:45,545
Damn right.

492
00:24:48,965 --> 00:24:50,675
I could've drowned you
at birth.

493
00:25:01,644 --> 00:25:02,687
Let's go.

494
00:25:02,937 --> 00:25:03,980
Go where?

495
00:25:04,105 --> 00:25:06,399
- See my grandson.
- Uh... No.

496
00:25:10,194 --> 00:25:12,238
Okay, yeah.
We could do that.

497
00:25:13,990 --> 00:25:15,408
You're gonna have to buy
these beers.

498
00:25:16,910 --> 00:25:18,703
Huh. I'm paying, huh?

499
00:25:21,581 --> 00:25:24,000
- Son...
- Hey, call 911. Right now.

500
00:25:25,418 --> 00:25:26,461
Dad.

501
00:25:28,421 --> 00:25:29,464
Hold on.

502
00:25:31,758 --> 00:25:33,468
No. Fight it.

503
00:25:36,262 --> 00:25:37,347
Come on.

504
00:25:38,056 --> 00:25:39,098
Dad.

505
00:25:39,891 --> 00:25:41,726
Fight. You fight it.

506
00:25:44,145 --> 00:25:45,188
No!

507
00:25:48,232 --> 00:25:54,405
"Ain't it a cold, cold world?"

508
00:26:13,530 --> 00:26:14,573
Wayne.

509
00:26:22,039 --> 00:26:24,083
Rigsby, I am so sorry.

510
00:26:25,084 --> 00:26:26,126
Thanks.

511
00:26:26,293 --> 00:26:28,420
We are gonna find
whoever did this.

512
00:26:28,754 --> 00:26:29,797
Trust me.

513
00:26:30,130 --> 00:26:31,173
Yeah.

514
00:26:33,258 --> 00:26:35,302
You're on bereavement leave,
starting now.

515
00:26:35,844 --> 00:26:37,888
We'll give you a call
if we catch a break in the case.

516
00:26:40,265 --> 00:26:41,308
Okay.

517
00:26:43,102 --> 00:26:44,144
Thanks, everyone.

518
00:26:51,777 --> 00:26:52,820
Hey.

519
00:26:54,071 --> 00:26:55,614
I know what you wanna do.
You can't do it.

520
00:26:55,906 --> 00:26:57,074
If I got shot, he would've
found the man

521
00:26:57,241 --> 00:26:58,492
who pulled the trigger
and taken care of it.

522
00:26:58,784 --> 00:27:00,119
You didn't like growing up
with a dad in jail?

523
00:27:01,203 --> 00:27:02,746
Ben wouldn't like it, either.

524
00:27:05,999 --> 00:27:07,042
I'm sorry.

525
00:27:12,131 --> 00:27:13,173
Cho's right.

526
00:27:14,007 --> 00:27:15,050
Leave it to us.

527
00:27:23,142 --> 00:27:24,184
Hey.

528
00:27:24,309 --> 00:27:27,062
Hey. Van Pelt said that there's
no other big gangs in town.

529
00:27:27,187 --> 00:27:29,189
The Overtons and the Low-Riders
drove 'em outta business.

530
00:27:29,731 --> 00:27:30,774
Who told her that?

531
00:27:30,899 --> 00:27:31,942
Some guy that runs a gym.

532
00:27:32,067 --> 00:27:33,735
He pulls gang members
off the street.

533
00:27:34,111 --> 00:27:36,655
Let me guess--
is he a former crook made good?

534
00:27:37,072 --> 00:27:38,115
Yeah, I guess so.

535
00:27:39,116 --> 00:27:40,159
We should pay him a visit.

536
00:27:40,451 --> 00:27:42,369
Maybe she's not asking him
the right questions.

537
00:27:46,498 --> 00:27:48,709
When you step in that cage

538
00:27:49,877 --> 00:27:51,086
you'll be fighting
for your life.

539
00:27:51,211 --> 00:27:54,339
I'm not gonna put you in that cage
unless you're properly armed.

540
00:27:55,132 --> 00:27:56,175
These are your weapons.

541
00:27:56,300 --> 00:27:58,510
Right now, I'm teaching you
how to fire your weapons.

542
00:28:00,471 --> 00:28:01,722
Three-round burst.

543
00:28:02,055 --> 00:28:03,223
There you go.
Get your shoulder up.

544
00:28:03,599 --> 00:28:05,225
Get the shoulder up on the jab.
There you go.

545
00:28:05,767 --> 00:28:07,019
Come on.
Give me some.

546
00:28:08,020 --> 00:28:09,062
Fletcher Moss?

547
00:28:09,396 --> 00:28:11,982
Hi, I'm Agent Lisbon with the CBI.
This is Patrick Jane.

548
00:28:12,357 --> 00:28:13,734
- Hey. Good.
- How you doing?

549
00:28:14,067 --> 00:28:16,195
Agent Van Pelt said
you were really helpful.

550
00:28:16,487 --> 00:28:17,529
What can I do for you?

551
00:28:17,654 --> 00:28:19,072
Well, it's quite a setup
you have here.

552
00:28:19,448 --> 00:28:20,908
Yeah, you know, I'm just trying
to give these guys

553
00:28:21,116 --> 00:28:23,118
a little place to go
before they get in too deep.

554
00:28:23,494 --> 00:28:25,746
We think Huff's death
might trigger another war

555
00:28:25,871 --> 00:28:27,789
between the Overtons
and the Low-Riders.

556
00:28:28,665 --> 00:28:31,210
Is there a third player in town
that might be behind it?

557
00:28:31,793 --> 00:28:33,712
- No. Those...
- Well, actually, we're thinking--

558
00:28:33,879 --> 00:28:35,172
well, I'm--I'm thinking

559
00:28:35,631 --> 00:28:37,341
someone ought to just sit down
with these two gangs

560
00:28:37,466 --> 00:28:39,092
and have them talk it out.
What do you say?

561
00:28:41,178 --> 00:28:42,221
That's nuts.

562
00:28:44,264 --> 00:28:46,016
Low-Riders killed Sue's husband.

563
00:28:46,850 --> 00:28:48,685
Overtons killed Beltran's little brother.
Those guys hate each other.

564
00:28:48,810 --> 00:28:51,939
They're not sitting down
across from each other, ever.

565
00:28:52,940 --> 00:28:55,150
This gym is neutral territory, right?

566
00:28:55,609 --> 00:28:57,819
So what if we held the meeting here?

567
00:28:58,820 --> 00:29:01,031
But they're not talking,
so you'd be wasting your time.

568
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:02,866
It's worth a try.
If I can arrange it

569
00:29:03,367 --> 00:29:05,702
would you be okay if we held
that meeting right here?

570
00:29:05,953 --> 00:29:07,246
Could save a lot of lives.

571
00:29:07,621 --> 00:29:09,081
- Go ahead. Try.
- Thank you.

572
00:29:15,295 --> 00:29:16,755
What was that about?

573
00:29:17,089 --> 00:29:18,549
We need to get back
to the Overtons.

574
00:29:19,299 --> 00:29:20,592
Uh, actually, I'll go alone.

575
00:29:20,842 --> 00:29:22,928
- You're a little too cop.
- Too cop?

576
00:29:23,679 --> 00:29:25,013
Van Pelt. Yeah.

577
00:29:25,138 --> 00:29:27,599
I need to get something delivered
to Carson Springs.

578
00:29:27,849 --> 00:29:29,059
No, doesn't matter what it is

579
00:29:29,184 --> 00:29:31,603
as long as it's big, heavy,
and on the back of a truck.

580
00:29:32,521 --> 00:29:34,690
Okay. Call me
when you're done. Bye.

581
00:29:39,987 --> 00:29:41,613
I thought we'd said our piece
to each other.

582
00:29:41,738 --> 00:29:44,408
And I thought it was about time
we started talking straight.

583
00:29:45,284 --> 00:29:46,743
I have a proposition.

584
00:29:49,496 --> 00:29:50,539
There's a Low-Rider

585
00:29:51,748 --> 00:29:54,293
that's ready to give up
his gang to the CBI.

586
00:29:55,168 --> 00:29:56,211
Whole gang.

587
00:29:56,378 --> 00:30:00,674
But he needs to know that when
the other Low-Riders go down

588
00:30:01,466 --> 00:30:02,884
you will give him a job.

589
00:30:03,468 --> 00:30:04,595
Why should I trust you?

590
00:30:04,761 --> 00:30:06,430
Well, I'm not asking you
to do anything illegal

591
00:30:06,555 --> 00:30:08,473
I'm just saying
you'll give the guy a job.

592
00:30:08,765 --> 00:30:11,351
Doing what, I don't--
I don't need to know.

593
00:30:11,560 --> 00:30:12,603
This is a bunch of crap.

594
00:30:13,770 --> 00:30:16,815
The Low-Riders have ordered
a substantial supply of guns.

595
00:30:17,190 --> 00:30:19,735
The supplier's supposed to arrive
at noon today.

596
00:30:21,069 --> 00:30:22,613
- What kind of guns?
- I don't know.

597
00:30:22,821 --> 00:30:24,823
I-I know nothing about guns.

598
00:30:25,324 --> 00:30:27,159
All I'm asking
is that you check it out.

599
00:30:27,284 --> 00:30:30,078
If the information is correct,
you give this guy a shot.

600
00:30:30,370 --> 00:30:31,413
I wanna meet him.

601
00:30:32,289 --> 00:30:34,041
I wanna see
this informant in the flesh.

602
00:30:34,374 --> 00:30:36,293
Yes, well, that could
be difficult.

603
00:30:36,418 --> 00:30:38,086
I wanna meet him,
or there's no deal!

604
00:30:39,046 --> 00:30:40,380
Okay. Well...

605
00:30:41,590 --> 00:30:43,216
Well, I will see what I can do.

606
00:30:49,556 --> 00:30:52,100
Check out this gun business.
From a distance.

607
00:30:57,856 --> 00:30:59,524
It's 12:30. They're not getting
any shipment.

608
00:31:01,943 --> 00:31:03,236
So that cop wasn't on the level?

609
00:31:04,363 --> 00:31:06,114
He seem on the level to you?

610
00:31:06,573 --> 00:31:08,325
- No.
- This is a waste of time.

611
00:31:12,746 --> 00:31:13,830
Son of a bitch.
There it is.

612
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:18,251
Call Sue. Let her know.

613
00:31:23,965 --> 00:31:26,468
Okay. So they're out there.

614
00:31:26,843 --> 00:31:28,178
They're spying on me.
So what?

615
00:31:28,387 --> 00:31:31,056
Well, it means our informant
in the Overtons is telling the truth.

616
00:31:31,598 --> 00:31:32,891
So he's part of their family?

617
00:31:34,601 --> 00:31:36,144
And he'll give them all up
as long as I promise

618
00:31:36,269 --> 00:31:39,106
- to hook him up afterwards?
- That's the deal.

619
00:31:40,232 --> 00:31:41,274
I wanna meet him.

620
00:31:41,483 --> 00:31:43,443
- Uh, I don't know.
- Then forget it.

621
00:31:44,319 --> 00:31:46,071
Okay.
Well, I'll see what I can do.

622
00:31:46,446 --> 00:31:47,489
Hey, boss.

623
00:31:47,656 --> 00:31:50,325
There's some dude out back
with a flatbed full of scrap metal.

624
00:31:50,450 --> 00:31:51,493
What?

625
00:31:51,618 --> 00:31:53,620
I gotta take that.
I, uh...

626
00:31:54,830 --> 00:31:56,540
I'll set up the meeting
and I'll get back to you, okay?

627
00:32:16,685 --> 00:32:18,270
Hey, guys!
Glad you could make it.

628
00:32:18,562 --> 00:32:19,604
Follow me.

629
00:32:25,152 --> 00:32:27,112
This better not be
a waste of my time.

630
00:32:33,827 --> 00:32:35,829
We're not off
to the greatest of starts.

631
00:32:52,701 --> 00:32:53,744
What are you doing here?

632
00:32:54,370 --> 00:32:55,412
Has it started yet?

633
00:32:55,829 --> 00:32:57,831
It's happening right now.
You should be at home.

634
00:32:58,707 --> 00:33:00,542
- I'm here.
- You sure?

635
00:33:02,378 --> 00:33:03,420
Yeah.

636
00:33:05,964 --> 00:33:07,341
They should all be
in the office by now.

637
00:33:07,633 --> 00:33:08,676
Thanks.

638
00:33:11,387 --> 00:33:14,139
All right. Everybody settle down.
We're not gonna do this here.

639
00:33:14,473 --> 00:33:15,974
I thought you said
you were gonna bust them.

640
00:33:16,433 --> 00:33:18,394
Yeah, well, uh, I-I told them

641
00:33:18,644 --> 00:33:20,354
exactly the same thing
about you.

642
00:33:20,854 --> 00:33:22,856
Uh, big lie on my part.
I'm sorry.

643
00:33:23,023 --> 00:33:25,234
Just needed to get the two of you
in a room together.

644
00:33:25,359 --> 00:33:26,777
- Why?
- To stop the feud

645
00:33:26,902 --> 00:33:28,320
before anyone else gets killed.

646
00:33:28,487 --> 00:33:31,448
- You know Moss?
- Listen, my gym is neutral ground.

647
00:33:31,573 --> 00:33:32,616
You're safe here.

648
00:33:32,741 --> 00:33:34,785
He's very good at talking kids
outta making dumb decisions

649
00:33:34,910 --> 00:33:35,953
and, let's face it

650
00:33:36,578 --> 00:33:38,080
you guys are acting
like a couple of kids.

651
00:33:39,456 --> 00:33:42,209
- A sit-down.
- That's the idea. Give it a try.

652
00:33:42,710 --> 00:33:44,545
If it doesn't work, go nuts

653
00:33:44,712 --> 00:33:47,131
shoot each other all you like
just not when I'm there.

654
00:33:49,091 --> 00:33:50,134
What the hell?

655
00:33:54,722 --> 00:33:56,432
Let's go. Let 'em talk.

656
00:33:58,517 --> 00:33:59,560
Okay.

657
00:34:07,609 --> 00:34:08,652
You lie, woman.

658
00:34:10,028 --> 00:34:11,572
That park was open turf.

659
00:34:11,947 --> 00:34:14,116
Then we send my guy down there
your boys jumped him.

660
00:34:14,324 --> 00:34:16,034
Open turf?
That park is mine.

661
00:34:16,785 --> 00:34:18,412
So you paid a price
for trespassing

662
00:34:18,579 --> 00:34:20,831
and you kill my nephew
for payback?

663
00:34:21,373 --> 00:34:23,417
I know for a fact you pulled
that trigger yourself.

664
00:34:23,625 --> 00:34:25,043
You are one crazy old lady.

665
00:34:25,210 --> 00:34:27,045
You scum could never
learn your place.

666
00:34:27,171 --> 00:34:30,048
- I have given you the east--
- You ain't given me nothing!

667
00:34:30,424 --> 00:34:31,467
Okay?

668
00:34:33,051 --> 00:34:34,386
Who told you I pulled the trigger
on your nephew?

669
00:34:34,553 --> 00:34:36,555
This isn't how you do it.
We're here to talk about peace

670
00:34:36,805 --> 00:34:38,307
not dwell on he said-she said.

671
00:34:38,432 --> 00:34:40,768
Let's--let's dwell on it.
It's all very good.

672
00:34:41,018 --> 00:34:43,103
You're doing a lot of talking
you're not doing a lot of listening.

673
00:34:43,479 --> 00:34:44,772
Let's take the park situation.

674
00:34:44,897 --> 00:34:47,649
Beltran, you said
that it was open turf.

675
00:34:47,775 --> 00:34:48,817
Who told you that?

676
00:34:49,151 --> 00:34:50,277
I got my sources.

677
00:34:50,527 --> 00:34:52,321
Well, in this case,
your source was wrong, huh?

678
00:34:52,988 --> 00:34:54,031
Who's your source?

679
00:34:54,281 --> 00:34:55,449
That's none of your business.

680
00:34:56,116 --> 00:34:59,286
And who told you for a fact
that Beltran killed Huff?

681
00:35:06,794 --> 00:35:07,836
Damn.

682
00:35:10,380 --> 00:35:12,508
- Son of a bitch.
- Bingo.

683
00:35:13,258 --> 00:35:16,970
Now when you two criminal geniuses
are done killing each other

684
00:35:17,304 --> 00:35:20,140
Mr. Moss here and his new gang
are ready to take over.

685
00:35:20,474 --> 00:35:21,683
Son of a bitch.

686
00:35:21,850 --> 00:35:24,770
You killed my nephew,
and you blamed it on Beltran.

687
00:35:24,895 --> 00:35:25,979
Son of a bitch!

688
00:35:28,857 --> 00:35:29,983
You've got this wrong.

689
00:35:30,234 --> 00:35:32,194
I wouldn't do that if I were you.

690
00:35:34,112 --> 00:35:35,155
Drop the weapon!

691
00:36:22,452 --> 00:36:24,246
Police!
Drop the weapon!

692
00:36:24,746 --> 00:36:25,789
Do it now!

693
00:36:27,124 --> 00:36:28,250
I can't move, man.

694
00:36:30,294 --> 00:36:32,880
I can't feel my arms.
Please get me some help.

695
00:36:33,380 --> 00:36:35,883
Help me. Please help me.

696
00:36:39,177 --> 00:36:40,304
I said I can't move!

697
00:36:53,191 --> 00:36:54,401
Steven Rigsby says "hi."

698
00:37:21,011 --> 00:37:22,679
You'll get my report
when I'm finished.

699
00:37:23,221 --> 00:37:26,558
Until then, you will continue
with your paid suspension.

700
00:37:34,149 --> 00:37:35,484
You're free to go.

701
00:37:56,088 --> 00:37:57,756
You're gonna regret this someday.

702
00:37:57,923 --> 00:38:00,717
- What?
- Well, this. This paperwork.

703
00:38:01,301 --> 00:38:04,304
Every night you just file it
and forget it.

704
00:38:04,429 --> 00:38:06,264
You know--you know what it's like?
It's like...

705
00:38:06,640 --> 00:38:08,892
cooking a beautiful meal

706
00:38:09,142 --> 00:38:11,228
and putting it straight
in the refrigerator...

707
00:38:11,937 --> 00:38:12,980
forever.

708
00:38:13,146 --> 00:38:14,189
You could help.

709
00:38:14,815 --> 00:38:16,233
No, I couldn't.

710
00:38:19,361 --> 00:38:21,989
So... what's your report
gonna say?

711
00:38:22,280 --> 00:38:26,076
It will say that Agent Rigsby
acted appropriately

712
00:38:26,243 --> 00:38:30,539
and with sound judgment
when he used lethal force against Moss.

713
00:38:33,333 --> 00:38:34,376
Good work.

714
00:38:35,168 --> 00:38:36,586
- You got away with it.
- Me?

715
00:38:37,879 --> 00:38:38,922
Well, I can't make a case

716
00:38:39,297 --> 00:38:41,174
but you chose a remote location
for the meeting

717
00:38:41,299 --> 00:38:43,760
you set up a situation
where Moss had to flee.

718
00:38:44,594 --> 00:38:47,514
And there, by chance,
was Rigsby.

719
00:38:49,808 --> 00:38:52,978
Well, I'm--I'm flattered.
You--you flatter me, but, uh...

720
00:38:53,687 --> 00:38:55,230
I can't take credit for that.

721
00:38:55,439 --> 00:38:58,650
Moss didn't have to run.
I would've brought him in.

722
00:38:59,026 --> 00:39:02,821
The plan did require Moss to put
his own head in the noose.

723
00:39:03,113 --> 00:39:04,823
Small gamble
Jane had to make

724
00:39:05,657 --> 00:39:07,451
to keep everyone's
hands clean.

725
00:39:07,659 --> 00:39:10,328
- Moss fired his gun.
- So you all say.

726
00:39:10,954 --> 00:39:14,124
And of course,
Moss can't tell his version.

727
00:39:14,958 --> 00:39:20,380
And now Rigsby has taken
perfectly legal revenge

728
00:39:20,505 --> 00:39:22,174
against the man
who killed his father.

729
00:39:26,011 --> 00:39:28,221
Do you think it will affect him?

730
00:39:31,349 --> 00:39:34,770
Well, I think it's better to regret
something you did

731
00:39:34,895 --> 00:39:37,773
than something you...
didn't do.

732
00:39:38,440 --> 00:39:39,483
Perhaps.

733
00:39:42,110 --> 00:39:43,779
I suppose Rigsby will never know.

734
00:39:47,324 --> 00:39:50,368
Agent Lisbon,
my report will reflect

735
00:39:50,494 --> 00:39:51,828
that you made a mistake

736
00:39:51,953 --> 00:39:54,456
in calling Agent Rigsby to the scene.

737
00:39:55,165 --> 00:39:56,416
An error in judgment.

738
00:39:57,334 --> 00:39:58,376
Yes, sir, it was.

739
00:39:58,502 --> 00:40:00,545
- Yeah, Lisbon didn't call Rigsby. I did.
- Jane.

740
00:40:00,837 --> 00:40:01,880
Of course you did.

741
00:40:04,007 --> 00:40:07,302
Agent Lisbon, your instincts to protect
your team are admirable.

742
00:40:08,386 --> 00:40:10,555
And your biggest flaw.

743
00:40:11,556 --> 00:40:14,351
Yes, well, we all have our flaws.

744
00:40:15,852 --> 00:40:17,646
Don't we, Agent LaRoche?

745
00:40:21,274 --> 00:40:23,193
"I might have to leave you"

746
00:40:24,027 --> 00:40:25,821
"I think is what she said"

747
00:40:30,951 --> 00:40:38,166
"I wish I could sleep
'stead of tossing in bed"

748
00:40:40,168 --> 00:40:46,633
"I can find myself thinking
that I'd rather be dead"

749
00:40:48,426 --> 00:40:49,469
It's okay.

750
00:40:50,512 --> 00:40:54,975
"'Cause ain't it a cold, cold world?"

751
00:40:56,309 --> 00:41:01,523
"Ain't it a cold, cold world?"

